90
00:05:39,919 --> 00:05:43,812
Now, back to Nyasha. So here's the catch.

91
00:05:43,866 --> 00:05:48,119
When December pay comes early,
January pay doesn't.

92
00:05:48,159 --> 00:05:50,119
Standard Bank worked it out.

93
00:05:50,159 --> 00:05:52,519
If you're normally paid
at the end of the month,

94
00:05:52,559 --> 00:05:55,399
and December's salary
lands on the thirteenth,

95
00:05:55,439 --> 00:05:58,799
you wait forty-nine days for the next one.

96
00:05:58,879 --> 00:06:04,119
Forty-nine days. Seven weeks,
on one month's pay.

97
00:06:04,159 --> 00:06:06,759
Now put that next to Nyasha's December.

98
00:06:06,799 --> 00:06:12,359
She got paid, she sent money home, she
bought a bus ticket, and she bought gifts.

99
00:06:12,399 --> 00:06:14,519
All from the same pay.

100
00:06:14,559 --> 00:06:19,012
By the time she's back in Johannesburg
in January, the money is thin,

101
00:06:19,066 --> 00:06:22,439
and the next payday is still weeks away.

102
00:06:22,479 --> 00:06:25,679
Many people across South
Africa know that feeling.

103
00:06:25,759 --> 00:06:29,199
January can feel like the
longest month of the year.

104
00:06:30,162 --> 00:06:34,642
And there's one more cost hiding
in December: the price of sending.

105
00:06:35,202 --> 00:06:37,122
As we showed in our last video,

106
00:06:37,202 --> 00:06:42,482
the World Bank found that South Africa is
the most expensive country in the G20 to

107
00:06:42,562 --> 00:06:45,842
send money from.
In late twenty twenty-four,

108
00:06:45,922 --> 00:06:50,002
sending money from here cost
about twelve percent on average.

109
00:06:50,242 --> 00:06:52,922
The world average was
about six and a half.

110
00:06:53,202 --> 00:06:57,202
So when more money moves, more
of it can be lost along the way.

111
00:06:57,762 --> 00:07:01,202
That's why it's worth checking
the total before you pay.

112
00:07:01,442 --> 00:07:05,522
Not just the fee, but how much
will arrive on the other side.

113
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:08,562
So what can someone like Nyasha do?

114
00:07:08,642 --> 00:07:12,122
One: plan for January before December.

115
00:07:12,402 --> 00:07:14,482
If your December pay comes early,

116
00:07:14,562 --> 00:07:18,642
decide first what has to
last until the next payday.

117
00:07:18,802 --> 00:07:22,042
Two: send early, before the rush.

118
00:07:22,322 --> 00:07:26,882
Last year's border plan expected most people
to leave between the tenth and the end

119
00:07:26,962 --> 00:07:30,642
of December. Get your
money moving before that.

120
00:07:30,722 --> 00:07:34,482
Three: check what arrives,
not just what you pay.

121
00:07:34,962 --> 00:07:38,962
Ask how much your family
will get, in their currency.

122
00:07:39,042 --> 00:07:42,962
And four: remember that not
everything has to be cash.

123
00:07:43,202 --> 00:07:44,402
For many families,

124
00:07:44,482 --> 00:07:49,042
a top-up of airtime or data on
Christmas Day means they can call home.

125
00:07:49,682 --> 00:07:51,682
So where does it stand today?

126
00:07:52,002 --> 00:07:53,442
For this festive season,

127
00:07:53,522 --> 00:07:57,242
South Africa's border agency
has not yet announced its plan.

128
00:07:57,522 --> 00:08:00,842
Last year, it came out in
the first week of December.

129
00:08:01,122 --> 00:08:02,242
And by August,

130
00:08:02,322 --> 00:08:06,882
Zimbabwe's remittances this year were running
about twenty-two percent ahead of last

131
00:08:06,962 --> 00:08:10,162
year. So expect another big December.

132
00:08:10,402 --> 00:08:14,562
More buses, more queues,
and more money on the move.

133
00:08:14,882 --> 00:08:20,082
Let's recap. December is the busiest
time of the year to send money home.

134
00:08:20,402 --> 00:08:21,762
Last festive season,

135
00:08:21,842 --> 00:08:26,722
South Africa's borders counted more than
four point nine million travellers in five

136
00:08:26,802 --> 00:08:30,202
weeks. Why? Pay comes early.

137
00:08:30,482 --> 00:08:32,082
School starts in January.

138
00:08:32,562 --> 00:08:35,362
And the festive season
brings families together,

139
00:08:35,442 --> 00:08:38,482
or makes people send
something when they can't go.

140
00:08:38,802 --> 00:08:44,002
But December money has a catch:
a long wait until the next payday.

141
00:08:44,082 --> 00:08:48,002
So plan for January first,
send before the rush,

142
00:08:48,082 --> 00:08:50,642
and check what actually arrives.

143
00:08:50,722 --> 00:08:54,082
If you enjoyed this story,
subscribe for the next one.

144
00:08:54,122 --> 00:08:58,562
And if you're in South Africa, sending
airtime and data home this December,

145
00:08:58,642 --> 00:09:00,162
you know where to find us.

